{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/33289-captain-irving","id":33289,"title":"Captain Irving","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-19T10:33:44-08:00","id":33289,"title":"Captain Irving","content":"I've been watching Sleepy Hollow - and now I really feel the need to play (or include an npc if I'm storytelling) a Hunter character based on Captain Irving - someone who isn't driven by destiny, vengeance, or to uncover supernatural threats at all - just someone who WANTS to be a normal god-damn cop, but the supernatural keeps fucking happening, and he couldn't be more exacerbated with how RIDICULOUS it all is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T10:41:25-08:00","id":33298,"title":"","content":"I have always included some disbeliever NPC in any supernatural game. It has alternatively made players feel a bit humbled (&quot;Look, did you not just see me lift the car? And you think that it is just adrenaline?&quot;) and it also makes them feel comforted (&quot;Ok, so I am not the only one who thinks it is weird that those wolves are all glowing red eyes? Awesome.&quot;) but you just have to be careful how you portray the NPC. If you make him antagonistic to them, then they will see him as some enemy to be taken down as a threat. If you make him friendly, then he can be a nice breathe of fresh air in a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T11:03:48-08:00","id":33309,"title":"","content":"The thing I like about Irving is he's not the strereotypical &quot;disbeliever&quot; character. He doesn't refuse to act or go into irrational denial in reaction to things in front of his face. He's just annoyed that the supernatural has the audacity to exist, and make him deal with bizarre crap that he can't put in a report instead of the speeding tickets, liquor store robberies, and domestic disturbances that this job was supposed to entail. He's actually quite helpful to the very-PC-like main characters since does cover for them, makes stuff up for the reports, etc - so he can maintain a semblance of a normal police station and not get everyone fired and committed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T11:43:05-08:00","id":33321,"title":"","content":"You can have both, no problem. As long as you have the staunch opinion that in the end all can be explained by eans of science<br /> &quot;Well, inspector this seems to me an extraordinary case of parasitic infection. The behaviour and abilities the subject presented may<br /> look strange but is not stranger than any case of Cordyceps, I assure you. Blooddrinking? Well sure the parasite inside the subject<br /> is looking for ways to spread, no ? Vampires ? Small avian mammals, what of them ? &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:25:34-08:00","id":35897,"title":"","content":"I think what we are talking about here, though, is someone who wishes things were neat and explainable, but knows in his heart that they're not. And it just pisses him off.<br /> <br /> &quot;One thing about living in Santa Carla I never could stomach...<br /> All the damn vampires.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:35:22-08:00","id":36016,"title":"","content":"That's another good example, yeah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":